  "certified_type": {
    "category": "Indicator",
    "type_designations": ["PUE HY10"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Electronic indicator for non-automatic weighing instruments of accuracy class II and III, tested as a part of a weighing instrument. Maximum number of verification scale intervals n ≤ 6000; can be used for multi range weighing instruments; temperature range -10°C/+40°C. Stainless steel housing with 10.1\" TFT display with resistive touch panel; additional platform can be attached. Devices and functions: multi range, determination of stability of equilibrium, indication of stable equilibrium, zero indicator, initial zero setting ≤ 20% Max, zero tracking ≤ 4% Max, automatic zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, semi-automatic tare balancing (subtractive), calibration and set-up mode via switch on the main board, gravity factor set up, alibi memory. Interfaces: 2 × RS232, 2 × USB, Ethernet, 4IN/4OUT (per EN45501 5.3.6.1). List of additional modules: add. RS232, 4IN/4OUT (gland), 12IN/12OUT (gland), analog outputs (gland), PROFIBUS, RS485, CAN, Profinet, WiFi, external power supply. Optional memory module (Alibi memory) with embedded micro SD card per WELMEC 2.5 guideline, software running on Windows Embedded Compact 7, parameters per Test Report No. 6014-PT-S0027-10."
